# Netlify CLI working directory — deploy output and a generated copy of
# netlify.toml, rebuilt on every deploy. The real config is netlify.toml at
# the repo root.
.netlify

# Backups the dev asset writer leaves behind. An earlier build shipped a
# logo.png.bak inside the APK to every phone; once was enough.
*.bak

# A design-canvas export dropped here for local reference (a zip, exported
# images, generated support files) — not part of the app, never meant to be
# committed. Only this one folder; DOCUMENT GUIDES/ itself holds real
# reference docs that stay tracked. Files stay on disk; git just stops
# seeing them.
DOCUMENT GUIDES/New folder/

# Deploy archives. Both are outputs of a build that is itself ignored above,
# so committing them stored the same thing twice — once as source, once
# zipped — and neither copy is what the site actually serves.
/todasaferide-dist.zip
/todasaferide-cloudflare.zip

# Master artwork left in the repo root: six full-resolution logo files,
# ~10MB between them, none of them referenced by the app. What ships is
# public/logo.webp at 59KB, exported from these. They stay on disk as the
# originals to re-export from; git just stops carrying them.
/TODA RIDE LOGO.png
/TODASAFERIDE LOGO.JPG
/TODA SAFE RIDE -transparent logo.png
/TODA SAFE RIDE LOGO V3.png
/TODA SAFE RIDE LOGO V3-transparent.png
/TODA SAFE RIDE LOGO black.png

# Partner artwork sources dropped next to the RCSJGH master: the full
# Rotary/TODA banner design, the white-on-transparent Rotary wordmark, and
# two Rotary logo variants — ~2.5MB between them, none served by the app.
# What ships is partner-logo.png and partner-banner.webp in public/,
# exported from these. They stay on disk to re-export from; git stops
# carrying them, same as the root master logos above.
DOCUMENT GUIDES/operator logo/Rotary and todaride ogo design.png
DOCUMENT GUIDES/operator logo/Rotary Logo-white.png
DOCUMENT GUIDES/operator logo/Rotary Logo_EN21_DynamicSize_FontUpdate.jfif
DOCUMENT GUIDES/operator logo/Rotary Logo_Standard RCSJGH.png
